    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1291-a1">

                <pb facs="1028" n="912" xml:id="pg912"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        Hacienda</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1260.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-08-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I have the honor to
                    request that your excellency will be good enough to receive and give a hearing
                    to Mr. Thomas K. Eccles, Chairman, General Board of Adjustment for the Order of
                    Railway Conductors, National Railways of Mexico; Mr. H. H. Kasten, General
                    Chairman of the Grand Council of Adjustment, Brotherhood of Locomotive
                    Engineers, National Railways of Mexico; and the gentlemen who will accompany
                    them, who have represented to this Embassy that they fear a strike of
                    anti-American character by the Mexican employees of the National Railways, which
                    may seriously jeopardize their personal safety, about the middle of this month.
                    They also state that they are subjected to constant discrimination on account of
                    their nationality. I therefore harbor the conviction that your excellency will
                    be desirous of hearing at first hand what they have to say in regard to the
                    matters which have caused them to seek an audience with you, and I beg to assure
                    your excellency that the attention and consideration your excellency will show
                    them will be appreciated no less highly by them than by myself.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fred Morris Dearing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
